  "reason": "R1 and R3 directly establish that hybrid Monte Carlo/MD equilibration can generate chemical SRO in a closely similar bcc refractory HEA and that this ordering can alter properties, while R5 and R17 establish the relevant HfNbTaTiZr material and its random or metastable bcc state. Several other records provide weaker precedents for B2 ordering, nanoscale chemical clustering, coherent precipitates, or network-like second phases. However, none connects SRO in HfNbTaTiZr to lattice thermal conductivity, reduced lattice-distortion scattering, phonon-density-of-states changes, or high-conductivity percolation pathways. Thus the literature points toward computationally imposing SRO in this alloy family, but the specific thermal-transport mechanism and predicted conductivity enhancement require a substantial new idea."
